    },
    "body": "PR #1292 exposed a largely empty prefix-memory path, while the roadmap and README still scheduled the completed qualification task. This review scopes that result, records remaining argmax/gradient-reference and population-accounting defects, and selects an always-present learned exact-token context prior plus causal memory through one shared low-bit decoder.\n\nThe complete DeepSeek prompt specifies the small Rust implementation, matched prior-only/joint fits, exported integer-path controls and generations, predeclared continuation gates, full resource projection and protected delivery. It includes a targeted primary-literature refresh through 2026 and keeps distinctive geometric contribution unqualified. Historical receipts and owner policy remain preserved; no Rust source, model artifact or resource balance changes.\n\nValidation: git diff --check; claim-wording gate; 630 repository-local links (one existing historical file URI preserved); independent source/math review with the packed-storage and contextual-intervention corrections applied. No Rust build or model execution. The five queue compatibility acknowledgements are not tests.\n\nReferences #973, #820, #963, #964\n",
